From 6884da4eff6de6a51b261ee679a34bca97a232b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:01:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] WIP mmb: the general-purpose bf16-WMMA dequant weight
 GEMM (all weight types)

Squashed theme commit (14 originals): dense Q4_K/Q5_1 + the RDNA3 arch gate +
the per-weight-type fusion stand-down; routed Q4_K/Q5_1 (expert GLU + down) with
the RDNA3_5-default gate; IQ3_S routed experts (WTYPE 5, on-the-fly grid/sign);
the portable WMMA wrappers (RDNA4 no-op) so the multi-arch build compiles;
Q8_0 in the routed/GLU path; on-the-fly Q5_K/Q6_K (WTYPE 6/7); IQ4_XS
(WTYPE 8); Q3_K/IQ3_XXS (WTYPE 9/10); the gated MMB diagnostics; then the
structural line -- the A-panel double-buffered GLU tile, the v_perm bf16 RNE
pack, the IQ3_S A-panel dequant split, the tile-class threshold
(THRESH == BN_SMALL) and the load_regs IQ3_S field preload.
